## Linked issue

Refs nibiru-labs/openbot-roadmap#65 (M10 mobile parity, audit `docs/audits/openbot-mobile.md`). Findings 1, 7, 14 and 15 and three smaller gaps are here. Findings 4, 6, 9 and 10 were already fixed upstream. Findings 2, 3 and 12 need a new Team API capability and follow in their own PR.

## Type of change

- [ ] Bug fix
- [x] Small improvement or alignment, with no change to how a feature works
- [ ] New provider, MCP app, or connector
- [ ] Translation or documentation
- [ ] New feature or change to existing behavior (needs an approved issue)

## What changed

- Agent prompts with an interactive block (confirm, quick replies, choice, form) render as cards and are answered through `respondToPrompt`; the question fallback stays when there is no block (1).
- The chat header opens in-chat search over the loaded messages with next and previous, scroll to the match and highlight (14).
- Day separators and an unread divider at the read boundary for agent and channel chats (15).
- Dropped system markers are projected, with a marketplace suggestion card (7).
- `Stop and send`: stops the running turn through the existing interrupt route, then sends; a failed stop sends nothing.
- Messages are grouped like the desktop rule (one time and one sender name per run); a created or changed routine shows as a card that opens the routine screen.

Surfaces: `apps/mobile` and `@openbot/i18n`. No file under `packages/contracts`, `packages/team-client`, `src/main` or `src/backend` changed; no migration; no new dependency.

## Verification

- [x] Mobile parity E2E scripts under `scripts/` cover each item; `bun run --cwd apps/mobile typecheck` passed for every run on the executor hosts (rc 0).
- [x] No physical-device acceptance yet: signing, push and lifecycle checks on a phone remain open on #65.
- [x] The pre-commit hook passed.
- [x] No credentials, private data, generated output, or real user files are included.

## Risk and security impact

Phone UI only; it uses existing Team API routes (the interrupt route for Stop and send).

Model and harness: Codex gpt-6.1-terra, Cursor composer-2.5 and pi + MiniMax through openswarm; planner Claude Code.

